The guest kernels of QEMU 11.1's tests/tcg system tests for aarch64, used by
tests/tcg_run.rs and by the ruvm-cli tests. They are QEMU's own sources
(GPL-2.0-or-later), built unchanged and stripped:

  hello.gz      tests/tcg/multiarch/system/hello.c
  interrupt.gz  tests/tcg/multiarch/system/interrupt.c
  memory.gz     tests/tcg/multiarch/system/memory.c, with -DCHECK_UNALIGNED=1
  asid2.gz      tests/tcg/aarch64/system/asid2.c
  feat-xs.gz    tests/tcg/aarch64/system/feat-xs.c
  semiheap.gz   tests/tcg/aarch64/system/semiheap.c
  pauth-3.gz    tests/tcg/aarch64/system/pauth-3.c, with -march=armv8.3-a
  mte.gz        tests/tcg/aarch64/system/mte.S, with -march=armv8.5-a+memtag
  vtimer.gz     tests/tcg/aarch64/system/vtimer.c
  semiconsole.gz tests/tcg/aarch64/system/semiconsole.c
  rme_gdi.gz    tests/tcg/aarch64/system/rme_gdi.c
  gpc-test.gz   tests/tcg/aarch64/system/gpc-test.c, linked with a boot.S built
                with -DLOGGING_VECTOR_TABLE instead
  memory-sve.gz tests/tcg/multiarch/system/memory.c, with -DCHECK_UNALIGNED=1
                -march=armv8.1-a+sve -O3

each linked with tests/tcg/aarch64/system/boot.S, tests/tcg/minilib/printf.c
and tests/tcg/aarch64/system/kernel.ld, built on x86_64 Ubuntu 24.04 with
aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc 13.3.0 and GNU ld 2.42, the flags of
tests/tcg/aarch64/Makefile.softmmu-target (memory.c without -Werror, which
gcc 13 trips over):

  CFLAGS="-Wall -Werror -O0 -g -fno-strict-aliasing -nostdlib -ggdb \
      -isystem minilib -ffreestanding -fno-stack-protector"
  gcc -nostdlib -fno-stack-protector -ggdb -O0 -ffreestanding \
      -c printf.c -o printf.o
  gcc $CFLAGS -x assembler-with-cpp -Wa,--noexecstack -c boot.S -o boot.o
  gcc $CFLAGS TEST.c -o TEST -Wl,-Tkernel.ld -static -nostdlib printf.o \
      -lgcc boot.o
  strip TEST && gzip -9 -n TEST

asid2.out, semiheap.out and memory.out.gz are what qemu-system-aarch64 11.1
(Homebrew) writes to the semihosting chardev for them with

  qemu-system-aarch64 -monitor none -display none \
      -chardev file,path=TEST.out,id=output -M virt -cpu max -display none \
      -semihosting-config enable=on,target=native,chardev=output -kernel TEST

which exits with status 0 for all six. hello writes "Hello World\n";
interrupt and feat-xs write nothing.

The others run with the options of the Makefile's run- rules: pauth-3 on
-cpu max,pauth-qarma5=on (writes "OK\n"), mte on -M virt,mte=on (writes
nothing), vtimer on -M virt,virtualization=on -cpu cortex-a57 -smp 4 with
arg=2 (vtimer.out), gpc-test on -M virt,virtualization=on,secure=on
-cpu max,x-rme=on with arg=3 (gpc-test.out), rme_gdi like hello (writes
"SKIP: GDI not implemented\n"), memory-sve like memory (memory.out.gz).
semiconsole is manual only in QEMU; tcg_run.rs types "hello worldX" into
it. All exit with status 0, except that mte passes main's return value, the
address 0x40400000 of its tagged page, to SYS_EXIT; QEMU exits with that,
which the shell sees as 0.
